# .trivyignore — documented, time-boxed exceptions for Trivy scans (FR-005, research D3).
# The PR security check hard-fails on HIGH/CRITICAL vulns and committed secrets;
# add an exception here ONLY with a comment stating the CVE, why it can't be fixed yet,
# the owner, and a review-by date. Every entry weakens the gate — keep this list short.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX  # transitive via <pkg>, no fix upstream yet; review by 2026-09-01 (owner: @you)

GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2  # react-router-dom RSC-mode CSRF bypass. App is a plain client-side SPA using BrowserRouter/Routes/Route/Link/NavLink/Navigate/useParams only — no RSC, no data router, no server actions — vulnerable code path is unreachable. Fix requires react-router-dom depending on react-router>=8.3.0, but react-router-dom has not published any 8.x release yet (still pinned to 7.18.1 -> react-router@7.18.1); downgrading within 7.x instead reintroduces 14 other HIGH advisories (verified via `npm audit`). Review by 2026-09-01 (owner: Юлия Шевцова) — re-check whether react-router-dom has shipped an 8.x release.
